  "date_building_work_completed_under_previous_permission": null,
  "lapsed_date": "27/08/2029",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed development would result in the loss of a family-sized dwellinghouse, the need for which is clearly demonstrated in the development plan and supporting evidence base. While it would provide a dwelling in the form of an HMO, it fails to demonstrate that this meets an identified need or is in a sustainable location, and further would not provide an adequate quality of accommodation to support a high standard of living by means of the insufficient size of Bedrooms 2 and 5. The development would result in a loss of local amenity including to neighbouring occupiers through an increase in disturbance and comings and goings. The site is therefore not suitable for an HMO use. As such, the proposal is considered to have a detrimental impact on the borough&#39;s housing supply and is contrary to the following policies:&nbsp;National Planning Policy Framework (August, 2026)Policies D6, D14 and T4 of the London Plan (March, 2021)Policies SP3, SP8, DMD1, DMT1, DMH5 and DMSI3 of the Barking and Dagenham Local Plan (September, 2024)"
  ],
